The DRM variant and the Widevine module
---------------------------------------

Lucium is built in two ways from the same source. The standard build uses
the Electron of the Electron project. The DRM variant plays protected videos;
the builds the maintainer publishes are of that variant.

- The variant is built on the build of Electron published by castLabs
  ("Electron for Content Security", MIT licence like Electron). That binary is
  not rebuilt by this project; its checksum is compared with the one castLabs
  publishes. The built application is then signed by the signing service of
  castLabs (a "VMP" signature), which the video services ask for.
- Protected videos are decrypted by the Widevine Content Decryption Module, a
  proprietary program of Google. It is not free software.
- That module is not in this repository and not in the application this
  project hands out. The engine downloads it by itself, from the component
  service of its publisher, on the computer of the person who runs the
  variant, and keeps it up to date. Its terms are those of its publisher.
- No code of Lucium is linked with the module when the application is built.
  The engine loads it when it runs, behind the Encrypted Media Extensions
  interface of Chromium; Lucium only asks the engine to install it
  (src/main/engine/widevine.ts).
- The standard build neither contains nor downloads the module.

